WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.334 --> 00:00:19.367
Once all the children were settled in at Number 14, Mr. and Mrs. Darling signed the boys up for public school.

2
00:00:19.368 --> 00:00:26.204
The boys were in school only a few days before they started wishing they had never left the island of Neverland.

3
00:00:26.205 --> 00:00:33.868
But as time passed, they got used to their teachers and to learning everyday things like math and spelling.

4
00:00:33.869 --> 00:00:37.103
They settled down and became ordinary boys.

5
00:00:37.104 --> 00:00:41.740
No one outside the family ever knew about their magical past.

6
00:00:41.741 --> 00:00:44.966
Sometimes they went back to their old tricks.

7
00:00:44.967 --> 00:00:49.736
When no one was looking, they would fly after their hats on a windy day.

8
00:00:49.737 --> 00:00:56.785
Other times, they would pretend to fall off the school bus, only to fly safely away.

9
00:00:56.786 --> 00:01:03.138
At first, Nana tied their feet to the bedposts, so that they could not fly away at night.

10
00:01:03.139 --> 00:01:06.317
But soon they forgot how to fly at all.

11
00:01:06.318 --> 00:01:09.237
Maybe it was because they were out of practice.

12
00:01:09.238 --> 00:01:13.396
Or maybe it was just that they no longer believed they could.

13
00:01:13.397 --> 00:01:18.827
Being the youngest, Michael continued to believe longer than the other boys.

14
00:01:18.828 --> 00:01:22.011
He remembered Neverland for a long time.

15
00:01:22.012 --> 00:01:25.862
He was with Wendy when Peter came for her in the spring.

16
00:01:25.863 --> 00:01:31.781
Though Peter did not notice, both Michael and his sister had grown much taller.

17
00:01:31.782 --> 00:01:37.807
For Wendy, it had been a long wait, and she was excited to talk about the old times.

18
00:01:37.808 --> 00:01:41.188
But Peter was carefree as always.

19
00:01:41.189 --> 00:01:45.108
He only wanted to talk about his new adventures.

20
00:01:45.109 --> 00:01:51.262
"Who is Captain Hook?" he asked with interest when Wendy mentioned Peter's old enemy.

21
00:01:51.263 --> 00:01:58.054
"You don't remember how you killed him and saved all our lives?" she asked, amazed.

22
00:01:58.055 --> 00:02:02.834
"I forget them as soon as I've killed them," Peter replied.

23
00:02:02.835 --> 00:02:07.643
When Wendy asked about Tinker Bell, he didn't know who the fairy was.

24
00:02:07.644 --> 00:02:13.199
"Oh, Peter, how could you not remember?" she said in shock.

25
00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:18.964
"There are such a lot of fairies," he said, "and they don't live too long."

26
00:02:18.965 --> 00:02:25.057
But Wendy still loved Peter. To her, Peter was as fascinating as ever.

27
00:02:25.058 --> 00:02:32.002
And when they finally got to Neverland, they had a lovely spring cleaning in the little house in the treetops.

28
00:02:32.003 --> 00:02:38.850
The next year, Wendy waited at the window for days, but Peter did not come for her.

29
00:02:38.851 --> 00:02:42.215
"Maybe he's sick," said Michael.

30
00:02:42.216 --> 00:02:46.084
"You know he's never sick," she replied.

31
00:02:46.085 --> 00:02:54.561
Michael came closer and whispered sadly, "Wendy, maybe there is no such person as Peter Pan."

32
00:02:54.562 --> 00:03:00.088
Michael burst into tears when he said it. Wendy wanted to cry too.

33
00:03:00.089 --> 00:03:03.816
The following spring, Peter came for her.

34
00:03:03.817 --> 00:03:07.786
Strangely, he didn't remember that he had missed a year.

35
00:03:07.787 --> 00:03:12.842
When he brought her back home, he said, "Always be waiting here for me.

36
00:03:12.843 --> 00:03:15.888
Some night you will hear my crow.

37
00:03:15.889 --> 00:03:20.290
And I'll be there to bring you back to Neverland!"

38
00:03:20.291 --> 00:03:24.942
That was the last time the little girl named Wendy ever saw him.

39
00:03:24.943 --> 00:03:27.266
She tried not to grow up.

40
00:03:27.267 --> 00:03:37.574
She tried to be loyal to Peter, but as the years went by, Wendy did grow up, and Peter became a vague memory.

41
00:03:37.575 --> 00:03:42.953
All the boys grew up too. Nibs and Curly became teachers.

42
00:03:42.954 --> 00:03:45.864
Michael became an engineer.

43
00:03:45.865 --> 00:03:51.523
Slightly married a lady who was a medical doctor and he never had to work again.

44
00:03:51.524 --> 00:03:56.586
Tootles became a lawyer and then a judge.

45
00:03:56.587 --> 00:03:59.847
The twins owned a shipyard.

46
00:03:59.848 --> 00:04:06.663
Like his father, John worked at a bank and couldn't remember any stories to tell his children.

47
00:04:06.664 --> 00:04:13.791
And Wendy got married in a long white dress and became a real mother.
